-- Notes:
--  R1 (FALSE, default): skips 1xx informational, returns final 200 + body. Normal usage.
--  R2 (TRUE then FALSE): TRUE returns the 1xx (100 Continue); a following FALSE advances
--      to the final 200 + body. Correct two-step usage.
--  R3 (looping TRUE): the 1xx is not advanced/consumed; each get_response(TRUE) opens a new
--      request context without closing the previous, accumulating until the UTL_HTTP per-session
--      limit of open HTTP requests (default 5) is exceeded -> ORA-29270, raised and caught
--      normally by EXCEPTION. The trailing ORA-03113 is the session connection left unusable
--      (unclosed requests), not a server-process segfault. It is a session limit, not a "crash".
